    <article>
      <section><span class="section-label">Section 01</span><h2>Visible Failure</h2><div class="value">Nia Voss, the night QA supervisor, reported that test MR-17 began running Test K-44, an outdated test. After discovery, the operator sent a stop request/command at 02:14:02 which returned &quot;ACTIVE_INSTRUCTION_PENDING&quot; and kept repeating Test K-44. </div></section>
      <section><span class="section-label">Section 02</span><h2>Verified Facts</h2><div class="value">Fact 1 - Incident log shows at 02:14:02 the operator stop request returned &quot;ACTIVE_INSTRUCTION_PENDING&quot;. 
Fact 2 - Current scheduling console does not show Test K-44 in the current test catalog.
Fact 3 - Mara Ilyan confirms the pause of production in affected QA cell. </div></section>
      <section><span class="section-label">Section 03</span><h2>Assumptions and Open Questions</h2><div class="value">Question - Are we able to delete any traces of Test K-44?
Question - What is legacy_sync.exe? 
</div></section>
      <section><span class="section-label">Section 04</span><h2>System Environment Map</h2><div class="system-grid">
        <section><span class="section-label">Section 04A</span><h2>People and Roles</h2><div class="value">It seems that all workers in the QA cell are affected by the system. Nia Voss uses the system, Elias Chen supports the system, and Mara Ilyan manages the system. </div></section><section><span class="section-label">Section 04B</span><h2>Processes and Rules</h2><div class="value">The Current Scheduling Console controls the incident. </div></section>
        <section><span class="section-label">Section 04C</span><h2>Information and Data</h2><div class="value">The Incident Log, Current Scheduler, Maintenance Record, Command Telemetry, and Staff Statements are important to finding the root cause of the issue. </div></section><section><span class="section-label">Section 04D</span><h2>Technology and Tools</h2><div class="value">MR-17 supports the work. </div></section>
        <section><span class="section-label">Section 04E</span><h2>Environment and Constraints</h2><div class="value">Mara Ilyan the production operations manager. </div></section>
      </div></section>
      <section><span class="section-label">Section 05</span><h2>Investigation Boundary</h2><div class="boundary"><div><h3>Inside the Investigation</h3><div class="value">The team will examine the full software history. </div></div><div><h3>Outside for Now</h3><div class="value">Current evidence does not require a restart because it will clear the commands it&#039;s holding. </div></div></div></section>
      <section><span class="section-label">Section 06</span><h2>Organizational Impact</h2><div class="value">The QA cell and its workers are affected.</div></section>
      <section><span class="section-label">Section 07</span><h2>Problem Statement</h2><div class="value">The impact is a pause on production until the issue is resolved. </div></section>
